                   "Divide the dough in quarters and roll each piece into an oval about 9 inches long on floured parchment.",
                   "Roll the two long sides inward toward the middle, then pinch and twist the ends hard so each oval becomes an open boat with rolled rims.",
                   "Fill each boat with the cheese mixture, mounding it slightly, and pack some into the rolled rims so the crust bakes up cheese-lined.",
                   "Slide the boats, parchment and all, onto the hot stone and bake 12 to 15 minutes, until the crust is deep gold and the cheese bubbles and browns in spots.",
                   "Pull them out, immediately press a crater in each molten center and drop in a yolk and a pat of butter; the residual heat cooks the yolk to a sauce.",
                   "Serve at once, showing everyone the move: stir yolk and butter into the cheese, tear the crust ends off and dip.",
               ],
               note: "The yolk goes in after baking, never before; it must stay liquid enough to stir into the cheese, or the whole dipping ritual collapses.",
               shortcut: "Store pizza dough makes fine boats; the crumb is less tender, and you save the hour of rising for the part everyone remembers."),
        Recipe(dishID: "georgia-khinkali", serves: 4, prepMinutes: 60, cookMinutes: 20, difficulty: 3,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 cups", item: "all-purpose flour"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 cup", item: "cold water"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tsp", item: "salt, divided"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "8 oz", item: "ground beef"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "8 oz", item: "ground pork"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1", item: "onion, grated on the fine holes"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/2 tsp", item: "coarsely ground black pepper, plus more to serve"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 tsp", item: "ground coriander"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "dried summer savory or thyme (optional but Georgian)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3/4 cup", item: "cold beef broth or water, for the filling"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Knead the flour, cold water and 1 teaspoon of salt into a stiff, smooth dough, about 8 minutes, then cover and rest it 30 minutes.",
                   "Mix the beef, pork, grated onion, remaining salt, pepper, coriander and savory, then beat in the cold broth a splash at a time until the filling turns loose and sloppy; that liquid becomes the broth inside.",
                   "Roll the dough a scant eighth-inch thick and cut 4-inch circles; reroll scraps once. You should get 20 to 24 rounds.",
                   "Roll each circle a bit thinner at the edges than the center, put a heaping tablespoon of filling in the middle, and gather the rim into small accordion pleats.",
                   "Work around the circle pleating and pinching until closed, then twist the gathered top into a firm topknot; count your pleats if you want bragging rights.",
                   "Boil the khinkali in well-salted water in two batches, stirring once so nothing sticks, 8 to 9 minutes, until the dough is cooked through at the pleats.",
                   "Lift them out with a slotted spoon, dust heavily with black pepper and serve immediately, instructing everyone: hold the knob, bite the side, drink the broth first, leave the knob on the plate.",
               ],
               note: "The filling must be wet enough to alarm you; a firm, tidy filling gives you a dumpling with no broth, which in Georgia is a failed khinkali.",
               shortcut: "A tortilla press flattens the dough rounds fast, though you still need a pin to thin the edges where the pleats stack up."),
        Recipe(dishID: "georgia-satsivi", serves: 6, prepMinutes: 30, cookMinutes: 75, difficulty: 2,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 lb", item: "bone-in chicken thighs (or half a small turkey breast)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1", item: "onion, halved, plus 1 chopped fine"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tsp", item: "salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 cups", item: "walnuts"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "4 cloves", item: "garlic"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/2 tsp", item: "ground coriander"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "ground fenugreek (stand-in for blue fenugreek)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 tsp", item: "ground marigold (or 1/2 tsp turmeric plus a pinch of paprika)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/4 tsp", item: "cayenne"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tbsp", item: "white wine vinegar"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tbsp", item: "butter"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 loaf", item: "crusty bread, to serve"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Cover the chicken and halved onion with water, add 1 teaspoon of salt, and poach at a bare simmer 40 minutes, skimming, until the meat pulls easily from the bone.",
                   "Lift out the chicken, strain and reserve the broth, and pull the meat into large shreds, discarding skin and bones.",
                   "Grind the walnuts with the garlic and remaining salt in a food processor until they pass ground and start to look damp and pasty, scraping down twice.",
                   "Soften the chopped onion in the butter over medium-low heat until translucent, about 8 minutes, without letting it brown; brown onion muddies the sauce's pale color.",
                   "Stir the walnut paste, coriander, fenugreek, marigold and cayenne into the onions, then whisk in 3 cups of warm broth until the sauce is smooth and pourable.",
                   "Simmer gently 10 minutes, stirring, until it thickens to heavy-cream consistency and beads of walnut oil appear on the surface, then stir in the vinegar.",
                   "Fold in the chicken, take the pot off the heat and cool to room temperature, then refrigerate at least 4 hours or overnight; it must be served cold.",
                   "Taste after chilling and wake it up with a pinch more salt and a few drops of vinegar, then serve in shallow bowls with bread.",
               ],
               note: "Make it the day before without fail; the walnut sauce only knits together and turns velvet in the cold, and it thickens as it sits.",
               shortcut: "A rotisserie chicken plus boxed stock skips the poaching hour; the broth is thinner-flavored, so simmer the sauce a few minutes longer."),
        Recipe(dishID: "georgia-pkhali", serves: 6, prepMinutes: 30, cookMinutes: 10, difficulty: 1,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 lb", item: "fresh spinach (or 1 lb spinach and 1 lb beet greens for two colors)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/2 cups", item: "walnuts"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 cloves", item: "garlic"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1", item: "small onion, roughly chopped"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "ground coriander"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 tsp", item: "ground fenugreek (stand-in for blue fenugreek)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/4 tsp", item: "cayenne"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tbsp", item: "white wine vinegar"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 cup", item: "fresh cilantro, chopped"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 cup", item: "pomegranate seeds"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Blanch the spinach in batches in boiling salted water for 90 seconds, until fully wilted but still bright green, then plunge it straight into ice water.",
                   "Squeeze the cooled greens in your fists, hard and repeatedly, until no more liquid comes out; a watery pkhali will not hold its shape.",
                   "Grind the walnuts, garlic, onion, coriander, fenugreek, cayenne and salt in a food processor until the mixture is damp, fine and starting to clump.",
                   "Chop the squeezed greens fine with a knife, then pulse them into the walnut mixture with the vinegar and cilantro until evenly blended but not pureed.",
                   "Taste and adjust; it should land nutty first, then garlicky, with the vinegar arriving late. Chill the mixture 30 minutes so it firms.",
                   "Roll into golf-ball rounds with damp hands, flatten each slightly, press a thumbprint into the top and fill it with pomegranate seeds.",
                   "Arrange on a plate and serve cool or at room temperature with bread, at the start of the meal.",
               ],
               note: "Squeezing the greens dry is the whole game; every tablespoon of water left in the spinach is a pkhali ball that slumps on the plate.",
               shortcut: "Frozen chopped spinach, thawed and squeezed, skips blanching entirely and honestly loses very little; you still must wring it dry."),
        Recipe(dishID: "georgia-mtsvadi", serves: 4, prepMinutes: 20, cookMinutes: 25, difficulty: 1,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 lb", item: "boneless pork shoulder, cut in 1 1/2-inch chunks"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tbsp", item: "kosher salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "coarsely ground black pepper"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2", item: "red onions, one sliced paper thin, one quartered for the skewers"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 cup", item: "pomegranate seeds"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 cup", item: "tkemali sauce (or thin plum jam sharpened with lemon juice and a pinch of cayenne)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1", item: "flatbread or lavash, to serve"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tbsp", item: "red wine vinegar"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Toss the pork with the salt and pepper and let it sit at room temperature for 30 minutes; that dry salting is the entire traditional marinade.",
                   "Light a charcoal fire and let it burn to gray coals with no flame; add a few dry grapevine cuttings or fruit-wood chips if you can get them.",
                   "Toss the sliced onion with the vinegar and a pinch of salt and set it aside to soften while the meat cooks.",
                   "Thread the pork snugly onto long flat skewers, alternating with pieces of the quartered onion, keeping the chunks touching so they baste each other.",
                   "Grill over medium coals, turning a quarter turn every 4 to 5 minutes, about 18 to 22 minutes total, until deeply browned outside and just cooked at the center.",
                   "Rest the skewers 5 minutes on the lavash so the bread catches the juices, then push the meat off the skewers onto it.",
                   "Pile the vinegared onions and pomegranate seeds over the meat and serve with tkemali for dipping, tearing the juice-soaked bread as you go.",
               ],
               note: "Resist the marinade urge; salt, real coals and fruit-wood smoke are the flavor, and anything wet on the meat just steams the crust away.",
               shortcut: "A grill pan indoors gets you the crust in 15 minutes but none of the smoke; add a drop of liquid smoke to the onions, not the meat."),
        Recipe(dishID: "georgia-churchkhela", serves: 8, prepMinutes: 30, cookMinutes: 30, difficulty: 2,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 cups", item: "walnut halves, as unbroken as possible"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "4 cups", item: "100 percent grape juice (dark Concord tastes closest)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3/4 cup", item: "all-purpose flour"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tbsp", item: "sugar"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "a pinch", item: "salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "lemon juice"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Thread the walnut halves onto cotton kitchen twine with a large needle, making four strands about 8 inches long, each with a loop at the top for hanging.",
                   "Whisk 1 cup of the cold grape juice with the flour until completely lump free; this slurry is what thickens the dip.",
                   "Bring the remaining 3 cups of juice to a simmer with the sugar and salt, then whisk in the slurry and cook, stirring constantly, 10 to 12 minutes until it thickens to pudding and loses its raw flour taste.",
                   "Stir in the lemon juice, then let the mixture cool 5 minutes; it should coat a spoon thickly but still flow slowly off it.",
                   "Dip each walnut strand into the warm grape pudding, hold it up until it stops dripping, and hang it over a sheet pan from a cabinet knob or rack.",
                   "After 20 minutes, dip and hang each strand a second time for a thicker coat, using the leftover pudding, rewarmed briefly if it stiffens.",
                   "Hang the strands somewhere airy for 2 to 3 days, until the surface is dry and leathery to the touch, then slice into rounds; traditional versions dry for weeks, and this quick one stays softer and fresher-tasting.",
               ],
               note: "This is the honest fast version; real churchkhela dries for weeks until a matte skin forms, so expect yours chewier, softer and closer to grape pudding on a string.",
               shortcut: "Skip stringing entirely, stir the walnuts into the thickened juice and set it in a loaf pan; slice it like fudge, no hanging or waiting days."),
        Recipe(dishID: "georgia-lobio", serves: 6, prepMinutes: 15, cookMinutes: 110, difficulty: 2,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 lb", item: "dried red kidney beans, soaked overnight"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2", item: "onions, chopped fine"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 tbsp", item: "sunflower or olive oil"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "4 cloves", item: "garlic, minced"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/2 tsp", item: "ground coriander"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "ground fenugreek (stand-in for blue fenugreek)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 tsp", item: "cayenne"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tsp", item: "salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tbsp", item: "red wine vinegar"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 cup", item: "fresh cilantro, chopped"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1", item: "box corn muffin mix, baked as directed, or cornbread, to serve"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "a handful", item: "dill pickles, to serve"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Drain the soaked beans, cover them with 2 inches of fresh water in a heavy pot and boil hard for 10 minutes, then simmer 60 to 75 minutes until completely tender.",
                   "While the beans cook, fry the onions in the oil over medium heat until deeply golden, about 15 minutes, then add the garlic for the last 2 minutes.",
                   "Season the beans with the salt only once they are soft, and keep about 2 cups of their cooking liquid when you drain them.",
                   "Mash a third of the beans roughly against the pot with a wooden spoon, leaving the rest whole, and stir the onions in with a cup of the reserved liquid.",
                   "Add the coriander, fenugreek and cayenne and simmer 15 minutes, stirring and adding bean liquid as needed, until it is thick, creamy and barely pourable.",
                   "Stir in the vinegar and most of the cilantro off the heat, then taste; it should be savory and faintly bitter from fenugreek, with a sour lift at the end.",
                   "Serve hot in bowls with the rest of the cilantro on top, cornbread for dragging through it and pickles on the side.",
               ],
               note: "Salt the beans only after they soften and do not rush the simmer; underdone kidney beans are unpleasant at best and genuinely unsafe at worst.",
               shortcut: "Three 15-oz cans of kidney beans, drained, cut the cook time to 30 minutes; the stew is a little less creamy without the long-simmered bean liquid."),
        Recipe(dishID: "georgia-chikhirtma", serves: 4, prepMinutes: 15, cookMinutes: 70, difficulty: 2,
               ingredients: [
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 lb", item: "bone-in chicken thighs and drumsticks"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "8 cups", item: "water"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2", item: "large onions, chopped fine"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tbsp", item: "butter"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "2 tbsp", item: "all-purpose flour"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "4", item: "large egg yolks"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 tbsp", item: "white wine vinegar"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 1/2 tsp", item: "salt"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "a pinch", item: "saffron threads (or 1/4 tsp turmeric)"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 cup", item: "fresh cilantro, chopped"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 loaf", item: "crusty bread, to serve"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Simmer the chicken in the water with 1 teaspoon of salt for 45 minutes, skimming the first foam, until the meat is falling off the bone.",
                   "Lift out the chicken, strain the broth, and shred the meat into large pieces, discarding skin and bones.",
                   "Cook the onions in the butter in the rinsed pot over medium-low heat until completely soft and translucent, about 10 minutes, without browning.",
                   "Sprinkle the flour over the onions, stir 2 minutes, then whisk the broth back in gradually and simmer 10 minutes with the saffron and remaining salt.",
                   "Return the chicken to the pot and keep the soup at a bare quiver, not a boil.",
                   "Whisk the egg yolks with the vinegar in a bowl, then whisk in a ladle of hot broth, and another, to warm the yolks gently.",
                   "Take the pot off the heat and pour the yolk mixture in slowly, stirring the whole time; the soup will turn glossy and pale gold and thicken slightly.",
                   "Stir in the cilantro and serve straight away in deep bowls with bread; do not reboil it once the eggs are in, ever.",
               ],
               note: "Everything depends on the last two minutes: temper the yolks patiently and finish off the heat, because one hard bubble turns silk into egg-drop soup.",
               shortcut: "Boxed chicken stock plus a rotisserie chicken skips the 45-minute simmer; the broth is lighter, so be a touch bolder with the vinegar."),
    ]

